    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i finally did it. i got the promotion and the vp title i've been working 80 hour weeks for since i was twenty. it's everything i said i wanted. but i'm sitting here in my office looking at the view and i just... i feel nothing. it's like i reached the top of the mountain and there's just nothing there. it's actually kind of terrifying. what was the point of all that climbing if this is all that's waiting at the top?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your feeling of emptiness after achieving your goal is a common part of the \"arrival myth,\" where the struggle feels more meaningful than the result. Many leaders experience this shift because their worth became tied to the climb rather than their actual interaction or impact. Instead of viewing it as a mistake, try redefining the promotion as the start of a new journey where you can focus on building a team that shares your values. You now have the authority to design a career path that balances ambition with personal fulfillment and prevents future burnout.",
